# Every object in this repository is EVIDENCE and is addressed by SHA-256.
# With core.autocrlf active, text files were stored LF and checked out CRLF,
# so 12 of 494 .txt receipts failed byte-level verification against the
# manifest even though their content was identical. Measured:
#   local 1413 bytes  remote checkout 1454 bytes  delta 41 = one CR per line
#   remote normalised to LF reproduces the local SHA-256 exactly
# Content addressing is unsound unless the bytes round-trip, so all
# normalisation is disabled here.
* -text

